{
 "about": "Beta gate screens (the bars state wakes the bars like a user, by moving the pointer over the video; every other state wakes the bar it needs: over the current time (bottom) or the title (top), so a bar problem fails only the bars state) . gate.ps1 -Part screens: the main screens of the player: each opens, does one basic action and closes (each close variant, e.g. its button and Escape). Steps use the harness step format (README.md 'Step reference'); positions are logical px in a 1280x720 client area. 'should' says what the screenshots must show: the reviewer checks it in review.json. 'source' names the code the screen comes from.",
 "media": "mkv",
 "size": [1280, 720],
 "args": ["--start-paused", "--restore-playback-pos=0"],
 "reset": [{"keys": "{ESC}", "after": 300}],
 "states": [
  {
   "id": "bars",
   "title": "Player with both bars",
   "source": "player/qml/TopBar.qml, player/qml/ControlBar.qml",
